The ticket covers:
- the goal, which is to run the same pipeline on the EpicChurchSF sermons;
- an eight-step plan from inventory through Modal API and notebook to the quality check;
- the lessons we learned here;
- four open questions for you.

Those questions are which sermon metadata to search on, chunk length, whether to use the same LanceDB project, and the cost ceiling.

It links to the CMU project and the reference code in `cmu-database-group-lectures` and `epic-sermons`. I left out the full paste-in prompt because the ticket carries the same plan in a shorter form, and I can add the prompt as a comment if you want.

Linear had only one project matching "sermons", **Epic sermons v1**, so I used that. It's currently marked Low priority and Backlog. The ticket has no priority or assignee either, so tell me if you want those set.

